          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 9:1",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore, I contended with my brethren in the wilderness, for I would that our ruler should make a treaty with them; but he being an austere and a blood-thirsty man commanded that I should be slain; but I was rescued by the shedding of much blood; for father fought against father, and brother against brother, until the greater number of our army was destroyed in the wilderness; and we returned, those of us that were spared, to the land of Zarahemla, to relate that tale to their wives and their children.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 9:2",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And yet, I being over-zealous to inherit the land of our fathers, collected as many as were desirous to go up to possess the land, and started again on our journey into the wilderness to go up to the land; but we were smitten with famine and sore afflictions; for we were slow to remember the Lord our God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "Omni 1:27 (27–29); Mosiah 7:21."
          },
          {
            "start": 156,
            "end": 163,
            "text": "Mosiah 25:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Mosiah 25:5.",
            "prettyString": "Mosiah 25:5",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "mosiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 25,
                    "end": 25,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 5,
                        "end": 5
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 9:3",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Nevertheless, after many days’ wandering in the wilderness we pitched our tents in the place where our brethren were slain, which was near to the land of our fathers.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 9:4",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that I went again with four of my men into the city, in unto the king, that I might know of the disposition of the king, and that I might know if I might go in with my people and possess the land in peace.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 9:5",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And I went in unto the king, and he covenanted with me that I might possess the land of Lehi-Nephi, and the land of Shilom.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 98,
            "text": "2 Ne. 5:8; Mosiah 7:1 (1–4, 21)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 9:6",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And he also commanded that his people should depart out of the land, and I and my people went into the land that we might possess it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 9:7",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And we began to build buildings, and to repair the walls of the city, yea, even the walls of the city of Lehi-Nephi, and the city of Shilom.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 9:8",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And we began to till the ground, yea, even with all manner of seeds, with seeds of corn, and of wheat, and of barley, and with neas, and with sheum, and with seeds of all manner of fruits; and we did begin to multiply and prosper in the land.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "1 Ne. 8:1; Enos 1:21; Mosiah 10:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Ne. 8:1; Enos 1:21; Mosiah 10:4.",
            "prettyString": "1 Nephi 8:1; Enos 1:21; Mosiah 10:4",
            "references": [
