        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 9:10",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore it came to pass, that after we had dwelt in the land for the space of twelve years that king Laman began to grow uneasy, lest by any means my people should wax strong in the land, and that they could not overpower them and bring them into bondage.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 166,
            "end": 169,
            "text": "Ex. 1:9 (9–10)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 9:11",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Now they were a lazy and an idolatrous people; therefore they were desirous to bring us into bondage, that they might glut themselves with the labors of our hands; yea, that they might feast themselves upon the flocks of our fields.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "TG Laziness."
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "Enos 1:20. TG Idolatry."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Laziness.",
            "prettyString": "TG Laziness",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Laziness",
                "entryId": "tg-laziness",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 9:12",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore it came to pass that king Laman began to stir up his people that they should contend with my people; therefore there began to be wars and contentions in the land.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 9:13",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 9,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "For, in the thirteenth year of my reign in the land of Nephi, away on the south of the land of Shilom, when my people were watering and feeding their flocks, and tilling their lands, a numerous host of Lamanites came upon them and began to slay them, and to take off their flocks, and the corn of their fields.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 101,
            "text": "Mosiah 7:5; 11:12 (12–13)."
          },
          {
            "start": 136,
            "end": 143,
            "text": "Mosiah 10:21."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Mosiah 10:21.",
            "prettyString": "Mosiah 10:21",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
